A||||4||AkursedX||Few quick questions||||5||
Z||000000||AkursedX||12-02-2000||06:24 PM||||Ok, I am removing the decklid tomorrow to replace my plugs and wires and I have a couple quick questions...<BR>To remove the decklid, I only have to remove the 2 bolts on each hinge, that ground strap wire (I think this was only on 88's) and one other wire?  Anything else?<BR>My other question is that I am using 8mm wires, and I was wondering if it is ok to use the stock wire holders.  They fit in there, but they get pinched, I was just wondering if this would pose any problems.<P>Thanks in advance!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroJoe||12-02-2000||06:42 PM||||What kind of engine do you have?  And, most importantly, why do you need to remove the decklid to replace the plugs/wires?  I dont know about V6's, but in my I4 I had no trouble with the decklid getting in the way when I replaced the plugs.  You are right on with what bolts there are, but also there is the wiring to the latch for your AJAR light, and the long spring that holds the decklid up would also be a pain to get back on once you took it off.||||reg||4
Z||000002||Bob Englert||12-02-2000||06:47 PM||||You don't need to mess with the decklid spring to remove the trunk lid.  DO NOT attampt to mess with the spring.<P>While is is easy on the 4 cyl, many owners (myself included) find it easier to get to the front bank of plugs with the decklid removed.  Just mark the position of the lid with a scribe before removing.  <P>You will probably have to disconnect the wiring for the ajar light and power trunk release.  It is found by the passenger side hinge.  <P><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000003||AkursedX||12-02-2000||06:54 PM||||Yeah, i know to stay away from the decklid springs.  And yes, I have an '88 GT with a 2.8, and my big hands simply won't fit back there   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <BR>And thanks Bob for identifying what that "other" wire is.  I figured it was something like that but wasn't sure<p>[This message has been edited by AkursedX (edited 12-02-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||StuGood||12-03-2000||06:18 PM||||TGFASH (Thank God for average-sized hands)...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  I never bother to remove the lid just to change plugs.  But, everyone's different.<P>Just removed the rear decklid to do some semi-"major" work on my GT.  The most important tips I can think of are: 1} Mark the hinges for proper alignment on re-install,  2)Get somebody to help lift the decklid off.  Like a matress, it's not really heavy, but it's pretty  awkward for one person (generally), and,  3)Thread the bolts back into their holes in the decklid, so you don't lose them!       ||||reg||3
